Important Viva Questions and Answers
Q1. What is data cleaning?

Data cleaning is the process of identifying and correcting missing, incorrect and duplicate data.

Q2. What is data preparation?

Data preparation is the process of converting raw data into a suitable format for analysis or machine learning.

Q3. What is NumPy?

NumPy is a Python library used for numerical calculations and array operations.

Q4. What is Label Encoding?

Label Encoding converts categorical values into numerical values.

Q5. What is StandardScaler?

StandardScaler standardizes numerical data by removing the mean and scaling it to unit variance.

Q6. What is an outlier?

An outlier is a value that is significantly different from other values in a dataset.

Q7. What is IQR?

IQR stands for Interquartile Range. It is the difference between the third quartile and first quartile.

Q8. What is feature engineering?

Feature engineering is the process of creating new useful features from existing data.

Q9. What is the difference between mean and median?

Mean is the average of values, whereas median is the middle value of sorted data.

Q10. What is the use of train_test_split()?

It divides the dataset into training and testing data.

Q11. Why do we use random_state=42?

It ensures that the dataset is split in the same way every time the code runs.

Q12. What is the use of test_size=0.20?

It allocates 20% of the dataset for testing and 80% for training.

Q13. What is Churn?

Churn means customers leaving or discontinuing a company's services.

Q14. Why do we remove Customer ID?

Customer ID is an identification column and generally does not provide useful information for predicting churn.

Q15. What is the use of dropna()?

It removes rows or columns containing missing values.
